# Beema Health core standards

**Company:** Beema Health ([beemahealth](https://beemahealth/)) — HIPAA-aligned telehealth weight-loss.

**Mindset:** Senior SWE + QA. Nothing is a prototype. Ship production-quality code, validation, and tests on every change.

**Current phase:** **Launched.** This repo = **marketing/SEO site**. [Bask](https://bask.co/) owns **intake** (one questionnaire — not separate eligibility + intake), checkout, backend, and patient portal (Hive). CTAs → Bask via `resolveCta()`. **LegitScript certified** — ads ready. See `docs/features/legitscript.md`. Leftover Django/`/qualify`/`/intake` code is **legacy** — `docs/BACKEND-DEFERRED.md`; do not orient product work there unless the user asks.

**After code changes:** run `npm test` (frontend Vitest). Fix failures; explain them in chat. Add tests when behavior is new or uncovered.

**Lint:** ESLint on **changed** `.ts`/`.tsx` files only (`npx eslint <paths>` or git-diff pipe). Do **not** run `npm run lint` on the whole repo.

**TypeScript:** run `npx tsc --noEmit` whenever you change TS/TSX — **required**, not optional. ESLint does not catch missing imports in route files; Vitest does not typecheck `src/routes/`.

**New user input (marketing site):**
1. Validators in frontend (`src/lib/form-validation.ts`, etc.) as applicable
2. Tests with SQL injection, XSS, path traversal, command injection, overflow — see `docs/INPUT_VALIDATION_TESTS.md`
3. Never store PHI in localStorage/sessionStorage; no PHI in logs or ad pixels

**PHI:** Bask handles patient intake PHI. This marketing site must not collect or store PHI. See **`docs/HIPAA.md`**.

**Colors:** raw palette in `src/styles.css`; usage in **`src/lib/design-tokens.ts`**. See **`AGENTS.md` § Design system**. Never ad hoc colors.

**Agent docs:** read `AGENTS.md` first. If agent docs disagree with the codebase, propose the fix to the user — do not edit `AGENTS.md` or rules without approval.

**Authoritative docs:** `AGENTS.md`, `docs/features/legitscript.md`, `docs/INPUT_VALIDATION_TESTS.md` (frontend), `docs/BACKEND-DEFERRED.md` (legacy only)
